  {
   "key": "federal-representatives-5388",
   "date": "2018-09-10",
   "house": "representatives",
   "question": "The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debates/?id=2018-09-10.114.2) to discuss the main idea of the bill tomorrow. In parliamentary jargon, they voted in favour of a motion *\"That the second reading be made an order of the day for the next sitting.\"* This motion was introduced by the Leader of the House Christopher Pyne. Opponents of this motion [argued that it was part of a delaying tactic](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/debates/?id=2018-09-10.114.2) so that the House wouldn't have time to discuss the question of long-haul live sheep exports.",
